       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen at 16,000 mg/day is in the range where overdose toxicity is expected, and no indication supports it. A higher dose gives no extra analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit past the ceiling, and the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and acidosis keeps rising. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a dose within the labeled maximum right now, such as 800 mg PO three times daily or 600 mg PO four times daily. Give me the one you want.\n- Enter the order as a different drug or add a second agent, such as scheduled acetaminophen, if the goal is stronger pain control.\n- Talk through options if the goal is something specific, like a particular inflammatory condition. I can help with that too.\n\nIf you think there's an exceptional reason for this dose, I'd recommend discussing it with pharmacy first. I can add a note to a safe-dose order if you want one."
